It will be EINVAL if it has never been submitted. I would regard this as the same case as already processed.
So maybe 
```
int k_delayed_work_cancel(struct k_delayed_work *work)
{
	if (!work->work_q) {
		return -EINVAL;
	}
```
Should return -EALREADY?

I think that is easier to document.
EINVAL: work item is being processed and cannot be canceled.
EALRADY: Work item is not pending
